 in Week 11","description":"Saturday didn't offer much to change the season's complexion, but some coaches are coming under pressure.","published":"2026-11-15T08:17:38.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/page/gamedayfinal111426/week-11-top-games-highlights-takeaways","type":"Story","byline":"Kyle Bonagura","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Predicting the College Football Playoff: Who's most likely to make the field?","description":"Find out which teams our experts think will make this season's CFP.","published":"2026-11-15T07:48:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/page/playoffpredictions111426/cfp-predictions-week-11","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN Staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Lane Kiffin understands frustration as LSU's CFP hopes dashed with Texas loss","description":"Lane Kiffin said it was fair to question LSU's 6-4 record after Saturday's loss to Texas, a defeat that likely knocked the Tigers out of playoff contention.","published":"2026-11-15T15:44:48.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50488081/kiffin-understands-frustration-lsu-playoff-hopes-dashed","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Arch Manning leads game-winning drive as Texas stuns LSU","description":"Arch Manning found Raleek Brown for a 4-yard touchdown pass along the left sideline with 3 seconds left as Texas escaped Tiger Stadium with a victory over LSU","published":"2026-11-15T13:13:49.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50487515/arch-manning-leads-game-winning-drive-texas-stuns-lsu","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4819260/adam-trick","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adam_Trick"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Adam Trick","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adam_Trick","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:49Z","intro":"Adam Trick is an American college football linebacker for the Texas Tech Red Raiders. He previously played for the Miami RedHawks.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Trick attended Wayne High School in Huber Heights, Ohio. As a senior he had 65 tackles and two sacks. He committed to Miami University to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"After redshirting his first year at Miami in 2022, Trick played in all 14 games in 2023 and had six tackles. In 2024, he started three of 14 games, recording 37 tackles, 4.5 sacks and an interception. In 2025, Trick was named First-Team All-MAC after finishing with 59 tackles, 8.5 sacks and one interception over 13 starts. After the season, he entered the transfer portal and committed to Texas Tech University."}]}}